{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya","id":1503450,"title":"Awakening the Traditions: Sahajiya","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-19T08:21:38-08:00","id":1503450,"title":"Awakening the Traditions: Sahajiya","content":"I have been a fan of mage the Ascension for decades, but have recently come to realise that Awakening actually fits my gaming needs better.<br /> <br /> The thing I miss about Ascension, and the thing that I think provides a barrier to entry for many Ascension players is the rich thematic archetypes of the traditions.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I don't miss the traditions themselves (and it took me a long time to realise that) because they are a bit of a mess and don't really make sense in a lot of ways. In fact I have come to like the awakening setting much more than the Ascension one in pretty much every respect.<br /> <br /> The factions within the traditions however strike me as an excellent resource for legacies - and especially ones with strong themes that veterans of Ascension like me can easily latch on to.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I have decided to start revisiting the traditions and convert their factions into awakened legacies.<br /> <br /> I am starting with the Sahajiya for two reasons. Firstly because when I first played Ascension in my late teens sex, drugs, and rock n roll seemed like an excellent way to do magic; and secondly because they fit really well in the awakened metaphysics - they are basically thyrsus.<br /> <br /> There are a LOT of Sahajiya factions across various supplements, so I am going to stick to the ones from the core cult of ecstasy book for the time being, starting with the historical factions (because despite being the most problematic in some ways they are also the core of the tradition) and ignoring the political factions because they seem like pressure groups rather than magical legacies.<br /> <br /> I am going to take a look at each of the factions in turn. To start with I am not going to worry about specifics, I am just going to look at parent path, order (if one seems relevant), basic themes, and primary and secondary arcana for each faction. Once that is done I can go back and revisit them filling in details and creating specific attainments.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I am very new to awakening so would appreciate any and all assistance in this (clearly over ambitious) endeavour. All assistance, critique, advice, and guidance is welcomed with gratitude.<br /> <br /> EDIT;<br /> <br /> I am going to post links to the legacies here to make them easier to find;<br /> <br /> <b>Historical Legacies</b> <br /> The historical Legacies are the remnants of adjacent ecstatic cults. They were pushing the boundaries of acceptability in a time when values and availability were very different than they are today, leaving many of them struggling to find a place to fit their practices in the modern world without condemnation becoming witch hunts.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1503690#post1503690\">Erzuli Jingo</a> - mostly female voudun who use the blessings of the Erzuli Loa to provide healing from within the astral.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1503946#post1503946\">Fellowship of Pan</a> - Heirs to the ancient cults of Dionysus who seek supernal inspiration through drink, drugs, and hedonistic revelry.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1504191#post1504191\">Kiss of Astarte</a> - Preistesses of the ancient goddesses of sex and violence <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1504824#post1504824\">Maenads</a> - Savage preistesses officiating over wild rites that draw attention from the shadow.<br /> <br /> <br /> First up then:<br /> <br /> (With details from a wiki)<br /> <br /> Erzuli Jingo - mostly female voudunistas devote themselves to healing the minds of others by clearing their dreams with the help of their Loa, Madame Ezuli. Their magic involves astral travel and spirit channeling, and occasionally curses and other sorts of black magic.The Jingo call their arts with ecstatic dance, frenzied religious experiences, and fire.<br /> <br /> These seem to be clearly Thyrsus to me (like most ecstatic factions).<br /> <br /> I figure their primary arcana is probably mind for astral travel, healing minds, and clearing dreams. Much of their spirit channeling may be Goetic rather than strictly spirit as well. A secondary arcana could be spirit, although fate or even death might fit<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","user":"Tamuz","date":". 03-08-2023, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T08:45:14-08:00","id":1503452,"title":"","content":"I LOVE threads like this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T09:11:01-08:00","id":1503455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya#post1503450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These seem to be clearly Thyrsus to me (like most ecstatic factions).<br /> <br /> I figure their primary arcana is probably mind for astral travel, healing minds, and clearing dreams. Much of their spirit channeling may be Goetic rather than strictly spirit as well. A secondary arcana could be spirit, although fate or even death might fit</div> </div> </div> </div>Astral travel itself doesn't require Mind, and Astral Adept might be worthwhile merit to look at.<br /> <br /> Mind does all easier access to dreams, and maybe healing minds, though i'd like to see a group which focuses on healing minds with spirit /space (travel to the Oneiros, and then bind/kill the harmful goetia - drain them of essence, lock them away in a Space that didn't exist, so they can't harm the mind anymore...)<br /> <br /> But obviously using Mind makes certain things easier - though a rock in the Astral is still a rock (purview of Matter), as such a Goetic problem can be solved with other means... Life/ Spirit for healing/essence manipulations. Don't really know the original inspiration, so I'll leave it to you as to what route you prefer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T11:34:22-08:00","id":1503466,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your input, some interesting ideas there that I hadn't thought about.<br /> <br /> The original inspiration I think was voudun with an emphasis on rituals creating altered states (as with all ecstatics) and I suspect opening oneself up to possession by spirits/loa.<br /> <br /> I think that can be acheived by either spirit/mind/ or death in awakening depending on what kind of ephemeral entity you consider spirit to be.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of healing minds using something other than mind, because having scanned through the sahajiya factions a LOT of them seem to be based around mind in some way (and considerably less around time, which demonstrates one of the problems with the traditions being shoehorned into matching the spheres).<br /> <br /> Using a mix of spirit and life is an interesting thought, because those are the spheres listed as specialities for the faction. Needing to travel into the oneiros and heal or alter resonance might explain why they make use of astral travel so much. I clearly need to look into the rules and lore around astral travel.<br /> <br /> Is it unusual to have a legacy based around the ruling arcana of its parent path? Otherwise life and spirit might be a good match.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T12:15:00-08:00","id":1503473,"title":"","content":"Its not unusual, but its not incentivized, since you lose out on a third Ruling Arcanum and that makes a huge difference in your mana economy.<br /> <br /> You don't need Mind, but it is the most effective. Ultimately <i>Clear Thoughts</i> can just blast away most mental conditions, it allows summoning a goetia to confront your fears or deal with them via a controlled vision. Technically a Clavicularius who knows what they are doing is one of the best psychologists most people could wish for.<br /> <br /> In this case, it feels like a Thyrsus Legacy, one that is Time primary and Spirit optional. The Tradition was also called the Cult of Ecstasy because they used various methods to go beyond their senses, to hear the heartbeat of creation and adjust their perspective and thus alter reality. It actually makes a lot of sense, Time is how we frame reality, how we keep track of how things change. If your specialty is to reframe your view of reality, making adjustments to Time will be far more intuitive than any other Sphere.<br /> <br /> In this case, they may eschew Astral manipulation in favor of change via concrete, tangible actions. They use Time to help you figure out where to go in order to change course, then they use Spirit to help you perceive the zeitgeist of the moment and harness it to make the most of your chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-19-2023, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T13:25:10-08:00","id":1503485,"title":"","content":"If no one has referred you over to the Mage Translation Guide, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114433/Mage-Translation-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">here ya go</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T21:42:31-08:00","id":1503512,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I read the translation guide years ago, but can't really remember what was in it. I will revisit it.<br /> <br /> Time was the primary sphere for the tradition as a whole so I see what you are saying, but the same could be said about all the Sahajiya factions and im not sure that really fits the focus for all of its constituent factions.<br /> <br /> I think it is going to be difficult to nail down exact arcana until a clear picture emerges of specific attainments for the legacy.<br /> <br /> For now spirit seems likely, with place holders for life and mind (possibly time, but I want to look at what really sets these legacies apart). Spirit is mostly for the loa, but if they approach the loa as goetia then mind as a primary might work with life or even time as optional...<br /> <br /> I think nailing it down further might need some specifics, so a few thoughts on what shape the attainments will take might be needed. <br /> <br /> Looking up erzuli shows that it is a family of voudun loa with influence over love, women/feminity, childbirth and children, material love and prosperity, jealousy, and revenge. These loa are summoned into &quot;spirit horses&quot; so possession is a big part of what they do - either of themselves or of others. <br /> <br /> So looking at that, the mental hearing and astral work probably center around love and relationships in some way.<br /> <br /> I think I can see them operating through a mix of spirit/goetia summoning and entering the astral through dreams and trances to heal/ harm from there. I probably need to research the astral a bit more before settling on anything, but my instinct is mind with optional spirit. I like the idea of manipulating resonances as a subtle way of effecting changes.<br /> <br /> Time for some research...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-20T14:32:34-08:00","id":1503568,"title":"","content":"Having scanned through the 1st ed supplement about astral travel it seems that magic is not necessary in the process at all. Mind helps with various things in some ways, but none of those ways feel like they fit with the legacy (to me at least).<br /> <br /> In fact pretty much everything done within the oneiros seems best done by mundane skills.<br /> <br /> That means the Mages arcana (and attainments) should probably focus on what they do outside of the astral with a view to using it within as well.<br /> <br /> The erzuli have a lot to do with healing in various forms, as well as various incarnations of love so life feels like a good fit.<br /> <br /> I see them performing healings and such as well as entering, and helping others to enter, ecstatic trances in which the loa enter them for healing purposes.<br /> <br /> Spirit seems like a natural fit for these spirit &quot;possessions&quot;, however rather than traditional possession in which the spirit takes over and rides its &quot;horse&quot; I see the jingo summoning spirits to accompany them (or their subjects) into the oneiros as guides.<br /> <br /> Life magic and spirit numina should be able to be used to affect the emotional resonance of the dreamer, helping ease the journey within and make certain realms easier to find. It might also be possible for the spirit to assist the astral traveller with numena or possibly even help with skills checks.<br /> <br /> The spirit guides are probably chosen for the specific purpose of the journey.<br /> <br /> Is any of that possible?<br /> <br /> For the moment I will let it stand at that. Life for healing (and maybe harming through curses), and spirit for inviting/summoning loa spirits as guides into the oneiros.<br /> <br /> I especially like this solution because it matches up with the speciality spheres/arcana given.<br /> <br /> I don't know much about the orders, but with their focus on empowering and healing others I think they might fit best with the silver ladder.<br /> <br /> Next up: the Fellowship of Pan<br /> Inheritors of the legacy of the Cults of Dionysus, these Ecstatics believe that a human must embrace their primal nature in order to find Ecstasy. They believe mankind is at its purest when in the grip of its unconsciousness, such as when drunk or making love or art, and tries to capture and harmonize with this unconscious beat. They excel at healing, soothing minds, and inspiration. The Fellowship is rather loosely organized and for an Ecstatic Faction that's saying a lot.<br /> <br /> These are clearly Thyrsus.<br /> <br /> The speciality spheres are given as mind and life and I think these fit well. Life helps cope with their inebriated lifestyle as well as with healing and such. Mind helps Sooth others, give inspiration, and spread the intoxication to others. Mind is probably the primary arcana, with optional life.<br /> <br /> EDIT: giving it some thought, I think I like the idea of mind and fate better. Sorry of along the line of drunken boxing, with everything falling into place around them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","user":"Tamuz","date":". 02-22-2023, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T00:53:11-08:00","id":1503603,"title":"","content":"I am going to rattle through my first take on the factions as quickly as possible, so I can get started with actually drawing up the details of the legacies.<br /> <br /> Kiss of Astarte<br /> <br /> modern pagan sect with a Dianic foundation. Many of these are lesbians, and some even have ties with the Black Furies. Their rituals focus into healing, rejuvenation and retribution. <br /> <br /> I have no idea what to do with these. Astarte was a goddess of love, sexuality, war, and hunting. Probably healing as well, and is popular among modern pagans (hence being a modern sect I suppose).<br /> <br /> Their original specialty was spirit, but I think they fit well with life for the hunting and sexuality aspect. Going with that, I think life and spirit seem to be a likely combination for their attainments. <br /> <br /> Given their membership of the Sahajiya they are probably thyrsus, but I can see them fitting just as well as acanthus.<br /> <br /> They seem to fit best in the adamantine arrow.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bMaenads<br /> <br /> fierce and violent lot, even with their impressive and old legacy, the modern female followers of Dionysus have learnt to be more subtle and discreet than their ancestors. Still, every full moon they reunite to dance, revel and scream under the night, and even if some of them try to direct their rage killings into deserving targets, that is still quite subjective and many members fall into Jhor or Madness.<br /> <br /> Another group that seem to fit within the adamantine arrow. They also fit the Thyrsus well.<br /> <br /> These are the violent counterpart to the fellowship of Pan and I would probably give them a similar mix of mind and life (again, these were the original specialty spheres). Rather than the benevolent inspiration and healing given by pan however, the focus for these is on dragging people into their violent brand of madness and using life to enhance them into killing machines.<br /> clearly wisdom loss is a constant danger and they may even be left handed.<br /> Primary: mind, optional: life<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T02:52:16-08:00","id":1503607,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14453\" data-vbnamecard=\"14453\">Tamuz</a> good forum idea - Make collective topic for general project mantuance and general ideas - and then create topic for particular Legacy full write-up/detail discussion if it comes really deep in to. Project like tnie needs more General names, so they can easily be expanded upon - but you do not want to clutter <b>MtAw</b> subforum too much.<br /> <br /> For example to see how this topic project cam work - see<br /> <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a> by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12619_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12619\" data-vbnamecard=\"12619\">21C Hermit</a> </b><br /> \u200b<br /> For your project I may advise name like '<b>Awakening the Traditions - MtAsc Legacies'</b><br /> <br /> <b>Awakening the Traditions: Sahajiya </b>is misleading it will be only on one Tradition Legacy. OR you can ask mods to change topic name.<br /> <br /> On general note - I'm really interested in this project. I started to play with <b>Mage: the Ascension in 2003ish</b>, but found it too conflicting or sidelining in lore, and went with <b>Awakening</b> from there on. But all the subTraditions looked very nice for me and enticing in it to look them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-21-2023, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T03:33:00-08:00","id":1503611,"title":"","content":"I am unsure of your meaning about topics. are you suggesting Setting up different threads for each legacy?<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bMy plan was to keep everything (at least as far as the Sahajiya goes) in this thread and try to link the write ups in the first post as I complete them.<br /> <br /> If there is a better way, I am open to it.<br /> <br /> I am also open to changing the thread name if it is misleading - not sure how though. How do I contact the mods with a request?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T06:27:07-08:00","id":1503617,"title":"","content":"K'an Lu <br /> Taoist ecstatics dedicated to perfecting the self. The K'an Lu seek to perfect themselves, they aren't seeking to heal people or moving others towards enlightenment. They follow a decent portion of the Code of Ananda, but they seek to Ascend and free themselves from the Karmic cycle. They work to untie the Yin and the Yang principles within themselves to perfection. Few Cultist could stand the rigid structure of the K'an Lu's practice, though a few of their Taoist beliefs have made their way to the Western World. The Faction seems to be dying out and they are hunted relentlessly in their homeland of China by the government. Even so, they are considered one of the greatest masters within the Cult.<br /> they have extreme practices that seek a balance between the chaos of a world without boundaries, and the discipline of the trained mind and body.<br /> Specialty Sphere: Time, Prime, Mind<br /> <br /> Despite their extreme practices, their focus on seeking a balance between the chaos of a world without boundaries and the discipline of the trained mind and body suggests mastigos to me. <br /> <br /> In terms of arcana this is another one without much to go on. I can see a lot of possibilities: fate is suggested by untying karma and yin/Yang, but I think these are supposed to be more metaphorical and internal. Mind makes sense for self perfection, as would life. I am struggling to see where the suggested specialties of time and prime might fit but I am open to suggestions. My initial instinct is for a mastigos legacy with primary life and optional mind.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T03:17:55-08:00","id":1503672,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the fellowship of pan last night and the idea of drunken boxing kind of stuff came to mind - not necessarily as a martial art but the same idea taken to life in general, with them drunkenly bumbling along and everything falling into place around them. With that in mind I think fate is a better fit for them than life. I have edited the earlier post to keep the information in one place.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have also been giving a lot of consideration to the Erzuli Jingo and how to make them work the way I want. I am not sure that spirits can enter the oneiros and while imaginary spirits can be summoned within, they still don't seem to work the way I want. I am considering that mind may be a better fit, with a focus on summoning goetia as guides into the oneiros. I beleive they can also possess people and be bound into fetishes, so they do pretty much everything I need them to do but keep the thematic focus of the legacy firmly on the astral. I have not edited the earlier post yet because I am still getting my head around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T03:32:58-08:00","id":1503674,"title":"","content":"Next up the Vratyas<br /> <br /> Nepalese ecstatics who practice the deepest secrets of Tantric magic and live in seclusion. They militantly defend their ways from outsiders, including other Cultists. It is said that Sh'zar learned from the Vratyas, and that they possess a love for humanity as great as the Joybringers and a willingness to destroy as great as the Euthanatoi. They are taught from birth (and with magic even from conception) the secrets of the human body and how to unlock its utmost potential. Specialty Sphere: Life, Mind, Prime, Spirit<br /> <br /> Another faction with very little information about them. The text suggests a focus on life, especially as it pertains to the human body and unlocking it's potential. I can see them combining it with prime, but time could be a great addition as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> That completes the historical factions, and rather than push through the dissidents and modern factions first, I will pause here and start making some actual legacies while the ideas for these ones are fresh in my mind.<br /> <br /> I will create each legacy in a separate post and link them in the first post if I can work out how to do so, so people can get straight to them without having to wade through my brainstorming sessions first.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","user":"Tamuz","date":". 02-22-2023, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T10:04:09-08:00","id":1503683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1503611#post1503611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bMy plan was to keep everything (at least as far as the Sahajiya goes) in this thread and try to link the write ups in the first post as I complete them.<br /> <br /> If there is a better way, I am open to it.<br /> <br /> I am also open to changing the thread name if it is misleading - not sure how though. How do I contact the mods with a request?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not versed in Ascention lore - but not Sahajiya is ONE particular faction, not umbrella term for all Traditions offshoots in MtAsc? <br /> <br /> <b>You topic literally points to only </b><b>Sahajiya only in name. </b><br /> <br /> <b>Awakening the Traditions: Sahajiya</b><br /> <br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T10:21:40-08:00","id":1503684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1503683#post1503683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not versed in Ascention lore - but not Sahajiya is ONE particular faction, not umbrella term for all Traditions offshoots in MtAsc?<br /> <br /> <b>You topic literally points to only </b><b>Sahajiya only in name. </b><br /> <br /> <b>Awakening the Traditions: Sahajiya</b><br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren\u2019t all of these factions part of the Sahajiya aka the Cult of Ecstasy faction though? It\u2019s still on topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T11:41:34-08:00","id":1503689,"title":"","content":"Yeah basically the Sahajiya was one of the 9 traditions. It was originally known as the cult of ecstacy, but I prefer the new name.<br /> <br /> Despite being a single tradition, the Sahajiya consists of a number of internal factions or sub traditions. Identity tends to be stronger to the sub factions than the traditions, which act like alliances or coalitions of sorts.<br /> <br /> I have highlighted so far the historical factions within the Sahajiya. There are also a similar number each of progressive factions, dissonant factions, political factions, and yet more that are mentioned in places other than the core cult of ecstacy books.<br /> <br /> Each of the traditions is split into multiple internal factions in a similar way. <br /> <br /> Because of the number of factions/legacies involved, as well as the thematic differences, I think I will probably deal with different traditions in different threads if I ever get that far. Given that I have never created a single legacy and I am about to attempt a dozen of them just for the Sahajiya that might be a big if and/or take a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T11:57:56-08:00","id":1503690,"title":"","content":"So I have made a start on the Erzuli Jingo legacy. I am not sure how to make spirit work in the way I want it to, so I have settled on Mind primary with a focus on using Goetia as astral guides.<br /> <br /> Here are my initial thoughts, but it may change as I get a better understanding of both the arcana and the astral. I am open to suggestions: In particular it would be useful to have a way to enter the astral without needing specific locations - would this be possible with mind magic?<br /> <br /> EDIT: changes to yantra and oblations following advice from Temple Builder. Added attainments.<br /> <br /> Note: I am not entirely satisfied with the attainments, especially the mind attainments. As such I will probably revisit these one I have more experience with the system and practiced creating spells. <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Erzuli Jingo</b></u></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Origins</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Parenting</b>: Thyrsus, silver ladder?<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: The erzuli jingo are a historical legacy originating in the voudun cults of Western Africa and spreading to the western world along with the populations of slaves.<br /> They are still strong in Africa and have cults in the Americas and Haiti where similar beleifs have spread.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearances</b>:<br /> Preistesses called Mambo make up the majority of the legacy, although the occasional ismale houngan is not unknown. For the most part they tend to wear traditional African dress, and many carry herbs and fetishes.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine</b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: I am unsure. Probably spirit (2?) Along with dots in occult and medicine. Maybe intimidation, expression, and survival?<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b>: the initiate is taken on an astral journey through her oneiros and into the astral. she is introduced to the astral reflections of the loa and welcomes them into her oneiros.<br /> <br /> <b>Organisation</b>: mambo good regular meetings with voudun cults where they practice their rites and enter trances. The majority of these cults are made up of sleepers however. Meetings between awakened mambo take place on a regular basis to practice rites, assist each other in astral journeys, and train attainments.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory</b>: all creation is divine and therefore all creation contains the power of the divine. Spirits and Loa can be awakened in everything, and can then be reasoned with. By entering ecstatic trances near shrines dedicated to the Erzuli, the loa can be persuaded to enter worshippers minds and lead them deeper within themselves.<br /> By entering dreams through Ecstatic trances leading into the oneiros mambo can heal the minds of themselves and others, or punish transgressors for harm they have caused. The erzuli jingo call spirits to assist them on their astral journeys, often trading time in possession of a mortal body in return.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Magic</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcana</b>: Mind <b>optional: </b>life<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras</b>:<br /> Bags of herbs (+1)<br /> Fetishes (+2) - the fetish must contain a spirit with influence related to the spell<br /> Shrine dedicated to relevant loa (+2)<br /> Ecstatic dance (+2) - because of the nature of the trace and the time needed to work up to it, this can only be used for ritual casting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Oblations</b>:<br /> Entering the oneiros through Ecstatic trances, leading others into ecstatic states, nurturing relationships between others<br /> <br /> <b>First attainment </b>: Riding the Loa <br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Mind <br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: advanced duration<br /> <br /> <br /> The biggest problem with astral travel is that it leaves your body comatose. With enough time to prepare a mambo can attach part of her conscious to the loa, thereby split her consciousness between her body and her astral journey. This is only possible while not taking any strenuous physical actions in either world, meaning that the mage is forced to pause her actions in the astral in order to check in on her physical self, but it does mean her body is not left senseless. <br /> By preparing for a scene, the mambo can split her conscious thoughts into two tracks - one in the material world and one in the astral. She may perform extended tasks mental and social tasks at the same time in both the physical and astral worlds. Anything more strenuous such as performing a physical task, performing an instant task of any kind, or casting a spell causes her attention to be drawn away from the other world.<br /> This replicates the spell One mind, two thoughts.<br /> (I think it would work like this. It would be better with extra reach in order to expand what she can do, but that would bump it up the attainment list. at least it enables her to keep a check on her body).<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Life 1<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant casting<br /> <br /> Initiate Mambo are taught how to cleanse the body of toxins, allowing the subject a bonus equal to potency to resist the toxins effects for the duration of the spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Second attainment</b>: Erzuli's Protection<br /> <br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Mind 2<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: advanced duration<br /> <br /> Inviting the Loa to take possession of their minds allows Mambo to protect them from the attentions of others. By spending a scene in preparation, the Mambo gains a mental sheild that provokes a clash of wills against any goetia numina, influences, manifestations, mind spells, and supernatural abilities affecting the mind that target her.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Life 2<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant casting<br /> <br /> By channelling the power of the Loa, a mambo can purge her subjects body of diseases. Reduce the illness rating by the attainments potency. If this reduces it to 0 it eliminates the illness from the subject entirely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Third attainment</b>: Erzuli's Guidance<br /> <br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Mind 3<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: advanced duration<br /> <br /> After a scene of preparation, the mambo can harmonise her mind with the Erzuli Loa allowing them to guide her thoughts and granting her a bonus equal to potency in either a mental or social attribute for the attainments duration.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Life 3<br /> <b><i>Primary</i></b>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant casting<br /> <br /> Channeling the Loa, the Mambo heals 2 boxes of bashing injury per dot of potency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fourth attainment</b>: Bridge of the Loa<br /> <br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Mind 4<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: advanced duration<br /> <br /> With the aid of the Erzuli Loa, the mambo creates a dream bridge connecting her oneiros with that of her subject. This bridge functions as described in astral realms.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Life 4<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant casting<br /> <br /> The mambo is now capable of healing even lethal wounds, healing 2 lethal levels of injury for each dot of potency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fifth attainment</b>: Familiar Loa<br /> <br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Mind 5<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: advanced duration, instant casting.<br /> <br /> The Mambo creates a familiar bonded between a mage and a Goetia, who must both be subjects of the spell. The Goetia must not be greater than rank 2. The mage gains the Familiar merit, and the Goetia gains the Familiar manifestation condition for the duration of the attainment.<br /> Both parties must be willing and can end the bond if they wish.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","user":"Tamuz","date":". 02-24-2023, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T12:35:31-08:00","id":1503694,"title":"","content":"Now this is all my opinions, but I have made a few legacies before so maybe this will help.<br /> <br /> So, Legacies are made of Background, Oblations/Yantras, and Attainments. I\u2019d say you already have a solid background, so I\u2019m going focus on the other two for the most part.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d skip order parentage for now, until you have a solid grasp on their policies, and stuff. I\u2019d say they don\u2019t perfectly sound like Silver Ladder, because while they seem set up to act as spiritual leaders, they aren\u2019t really following the Ladder\u2019s policy on the relationship between Spirits and Humans, namely that humans should be in charge of the spirits. They might fit better in the Free Council or maybe even the Guardians<br /> <br /> One could use the Dream merit as a perquisite, along with mystery cult influence or something representative of being a spiritual leader.<br /> <br /> One could also use Spirit as the Optional, since Mind and Spirit actually work well together.<br /> <br /> As for Yantras:<br /> the herbs are fine as a +1<br /> Fetish use is neat.<br /> Shrine should be a +2, as locations are a universal yantra, and this is like specialized version of that.<br /> Dance is fine.<br /> Not sure where the cursing someone bit comes from, or why they would have particular influence there.<br /> Likewise, I\u2019m not sure where the fire bit comes from.<br /> <br /> I think you have too many Oblations, I think 3 is the rule of thumb. I like the entering the Oneiros one, since it actually can negate the cost of entry which is nice, and woks with their identity. Leading others in trance is good too, since it backs up their role of being a spiritual leader. The other three are kinda weak, in my opinion. Oblations should be an effort, and reinforce the legacy\u2019s mystical theme. They don\u2019t seem to do so very well from my perspective.<br /> <br /> Edit: I\u2019d put \u201cnurturing relationships between others\u201d as an Oblations, if I\u2019m understanding your previous commentary about them correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 02-22-2023, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T14:10:15-08:00","id":1503702,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your advice.<br /> <br /> I had gone with silver ladder on the basis of leading what are essentially cults. My understanding of the guardians is that they wouldn't think to highly of including sleepers in genuine music rites or encouraging possessions etc. I don't really understand the free council at all. I think you are right. I will omit any order links for the time being. <br /> <br /> Dream merit and mystery cult influence are good ideas for prerequisites. <br /> <br /> I have considered spirit as the optional arcana but I am not sure if it doubles up on the summoning side of things a bit much, with different types of ephemera. I don't see them making summoned entities manifest in particular other than through possession and fetishes. Are there any other ways in which spirit synergizes well? The logic behind life is for healing, but I am certainly open to spirit of it has more uses.<br /> <br /> Cursing and fire come from the initial description of them as a faction. They don't really fit thematically with the direction the legacy is taking however so I am fine to drop them. The same with most of the oblations. I will keep the two you suggest and I think &quot;nurturing relations between others&quot; nicely encapsulates the essential themes of the rest anyway so that makes a round 3.<br /> <br /> I will update in the Erzuli Jingo post once I have gotten my head around some attainments.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T17:47:59-08:00","id":1503708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1503702#post1503702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for your advice.</div> </div> </div> </div> No problem. Glad to help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1503702#post1503702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had gone with silver ladder on the basis of leading what are essentially cults. My understanding of the guardians is that they wouldn't think to highly of including sleepers in genuine music rites or encouraging possessions etc. I don't really understand the free council at all. I think you are right. I will omit any order links for the time being.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, it\u2019s weird. While you have correctly identified the style of the Ladder and the Guardians, the Guardians do make Labyrinths, which are basically are cults which are mostly fed lies, but with enough Truth that someone can awaken. As for the Ladder, they are basically radical humanists, and genuinely believe humanity should be gods. The Free Council is actually a spiritual throwback to Mage the Ascension\u2019s Traditions. They are all the minor Awakened orders banding together against tyranny. They tend to have stuff like basing one\u2019s magic on real life magical traditions and religions. And science and technology. They are weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1503702#post1503702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have considered spirit as the optional arcana but I am not sure if it doubles up on the summoning side of things a bit much, with different types of ephemera. I don't see them making summoned entities manifest in particular other than through possession and fetishes. Are there any other ways in which spirit synergizes well? The logic behind life is for healing, but I am certainly open to spirit of it has more uses.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mostly, it was Goetia lacking any manifestations without a spell, so if you are fine with that, then it\u2019s all good. I guess I forgot that you can bind Goetia to physical vessels with high enough Mind<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1503702#post1503702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cursing and fire come from the initial description of them as a faction. They don't really fit thematically with the direction the legacy is taking however so I am fine to drop them. The same with most of the oblations. I will keep the two you suggest and I think &quot;nurturing relations between others&quot; nicely encapsulates the essential themes of the rest anyway so that makes a round 3.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, I see. Well, I would say that any Mage can curse, and if you want to have a one off curse reference, the Attainments are as good a spot as any. And Life is better at precise curses than Spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1503702#post1503702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will update in the Erzuli Jingo post once I have gotten my head around some attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div> Cool. Good luck.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T07:59:21-08:00","id":1503756,"title":"","content":"So looking through attainments, I have a few questions.<br /> Firstly is there any way of entering the astral without being in a location that allows it? I can't see any spells that do it, but I feel like it should be possible. If it was a special attainment effect what rank would it need to be? (Note, ideally it should also allow the mage to assist others into the astral without needing to be at a specific location).<br /> <br /> I suppose it doesn't matter however as traditional voudun do use fetish- shrines for the place where they do their stuff, so needing to site these in specific places isn't much of a reach.<br /> <br /> The second problem I came across was either bringing goetia with you into the astral, or sending goetia into another's oneiros.<br /> <br /> I suppose they could get around sending into another's oneiros by bringing the goetia into their own and then using a bridge to take it send them into another's.<br /> <br /> The third problem I came across was the restrictions on reach for attainments. For a spell like summon goetia that feels like it should be a big part of what the legacy do, it pushes them back to the fourth or fifth attainment... I have thought of a few possible solutions for this<br /> <br /> A) most mambo rely on casting this as a rote. It is perfected as an attainment later in their careers.<br /> <br /> B)mambo do not generally summon goetia into the material world but enter the astral and deal with goetia from there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here are my initial thoughts on the primary attainments from mind:<br /> <br /> <b>First attainment</b><br /> <br /> One mind, two thoughts. Reach for advanced duration.<br /> The biggest problem with astral travel is that it leaves your body comatose. With enough time to prepare a mambo can split her consciousness between her body and her astral journey. This is only possible while not taking any strenuous physical actions in either world, meaning that the mage is forced to pause her actions in the astral in order to check in on her physical self, but it does mean her body is not left senseless.<br /> (I think it would work like this. It would be better with extra reach in order to expand what she can do, but that would bump it up the attainment list. at least it enables her to keep a check on her body).<br /> <br /> <b>Second attainment</b><br /> <br /> I have a number of thoughts on this:<br /> <br /> First is a mind version of the spirit spell: opener of the way. Altered in order to create an open condition for goetia instead of spirits. In order to work it probably needs to grant the ability to possess as well.<br /> <br /> The main issue is that a mage at this level has no way to get goetia Intu the material world to start with.<br /> <br /> Second is dream reaching. This can cause lucid dreaming. Can it be used to bring the mage or others to the astral? Can it be used to &quot;tag along&quot; on someone else's astral journey?<br /> <br /> Third is telepathy. I have seen it suggested that a telepathic link could be used to bring a goetia from the material into your oneiros.<br /> <br /> Fourth would be either a mind version of command spirit, tailored to command goetia, or psychic domination used for commanding goetia. The problem is that both are withstood (by rank and composure respectively) and would probably render the attainment ineffective.<br /> <br /> Fifth would simply be a mental sheild spell: invaluable for dealing with goetia and walking around in the astral.<br /> <br /> It looks like either dream reaching or telepathy are the best bets, but I am not sure yet which (if either) will be effective. Both can also be withstood meaning they would probably not work on anyone hostile, but they are more beneficent attainments anyway so it presumably shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> My instinct is that dream reaching is the most likely to be useful.<br /> <br /> <b>Third attainment</b><br /> <br /> <br /> I was hoping to use summon goetia as the third attainment, but unfortunately reach is needed to make it in any way practical so it will have to wait until later (if used at all). I suspect the legacy teaches it as a rote. (Could knowing a specific rote be a prerequisite?) It might be used from within astral space, but being withstood by the spirits rank severally limits it anyway.<br /> <br /> Sleep of the just looks interesting for helping someone into the meditative state necessary to enter the astral.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, augment mind or enhance skills would certainly be useful. Since literally summoning goetia is so hard to do as an attainment at this level, perhaps the loas assistance could come in the form of boosted abilities. Actually I quite like this.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth attainment</b><br /> <br /> This has to be creating a dream bridge, so that the mambo can enter another's oneiros. I just need to translate it to 2e.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth attainment</b><br /> <br /> I am tempted to put a higher version of Goetic summon here, but I think it is simply going to be inferior to a rote version at this point.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is a mind version of craft fetish with reach for advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Optional attainments</i></b><br /> <br /> <br /> The secondary optional function of healer is actually much easier to fill out with life spells: <br /> <b>First attainment</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Cleanse the body: the first step in healing is fighting off toxins<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Second attainment</b><br /> <br /> Purge illness<br /> <br /> <b>Third attainment</b><br /> <br /> Knit<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth attainment</b><br /> <br /> Mend<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth attainment</b><br /> <br /> Regenerate (reach for advanced duration)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","user":"Tamuz","date":". 02-23-2023, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T10:26:22-08:00","id":1503760,"title":"","content":"In order to gain access to the Astral without a Hallow, you would need a Making of Mind to open a mental gateway. In more practical terms, you would need the Astral Adept merit, which can be granted by a Ruling of Mind, but only to mages or Sleepwalkers. Another option is to use a Patterning of Mind and Spirit to grant the Gateway Manifestation to a spirit or goetia, which comes with its own logistical challenges.<br /> <br /> Regarding transporting goetia, normally you need to do a Goetic Summon from the destination point, which may require Reaching or ritual casting, plus a Hallow. Alternatively, they could Co-Locate the goetia using sympathetic range and Mind 3 to teleport then to or from the Astral. So basically the fortes of Mastigos, which I think would be a solid pick for parent Path.<br /> <br /> The restriction on Attainment Reach is the price paid for their consistency. Being able to ignore Dissonance, Disbelief, dispellation and not even have to roll dice means that a helpful Attainment can be a major addition to a character's toolkit. There is a homebrew rule that is often adopted and might be helpful, which is to add a meaningful restriction or complication to justify one extra Reach.<br /> <br /> Regarding Attainments, my suggestion is to distill the core idea of your Legacy into one phrase, with no commas or references. An example for the Tamers of Fire's beliefs being explained as &quot;The fires of the world and the flames of the spirit are one and the same&quot;, the Transhuman Engineers embodying the idea of &quot;Building the Singularity draws the Supernal and Fallen closer together&quot; and the Universal Harmony's philosophy being \u201cMusic is an agreeable harmony for the honor of God&quot;.<br /> <br /> Once you have that core phrase, filter your ideas through it, any Attainments that reinforce it are kept, any that do not synergize need to be reconsidered. That will help build a toolkit that builds on the themes.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-23-2023, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T06:30:31-08:00","id":1503804,"title":"","content":"I have added attainments and such to the Erzuli Jingo post.<br /> <br /> I am trying to put a link to the post in the first post so that it is easier to find, but I can't work out how.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know how to put a link to a post?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","user":"Tamuz","date":". 02-24-2023, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T07:22:06-08:00","id":1503808,"title":"","content":"See that little number on the top right hand of your post? Click it, and copy the url it brings up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T13:34:18-08:00","id":1503843,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I have got that to work.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your advice kaiserafini.<br /> <br /> The stuff about the astral is both useful and interesting. For the moment I think it might be saved for spells as I am going to stand back from this legacy for now while I gain a bit of experience. I think trying to get my head around so many systems at once was probably biting off more than I could chew.<br /> <br /> I think the ideas about bringing goetia in and out of the astral just had too many hurdles for me to make work at the moment. I have arrived at a compromise that I am sort of satisfied with for now.<br /> <br /> The restriction on reach is difficult for some concepts. I may end up using the houserule about adding a complication for an extra reach. It seems a fair compromise. <br /> <br /> Your suggestion to distil the core idea of the legacy into a single phrase is a good one and cuts to the heart of something that has been bothering me about these attainments. The optional life attainments stem from a completely different theme, and after I wrote them they started to look like a completely different legacy tacked on. I had already been considering removing them, and I think your advice has solidified that idea in my mind. I will consider other optional arcana that fit better with the core theme over time. Your suggestions about space seem wise, and spirit has a lot going for it as well.<br /> <br /> For now, I am going to move on. <br /> <br /> Next on the list are the Fellowship of Pan. They should be a bit easier due to both the fact that I actually have a clear idea what to do with them, and the fact that it shouldn't cross so many difficult systems.<br /> <br /> Starting with the core theme to filter everything through seems like a good idea:<br /> <br /> <i>Finding and sharing inspiration by filtering the supernal through intoxicated revelry.</i><br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T08:34:04-08:00","id":1503946,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>Fellowship of Pan</b></u></span></div> <br /> <u><b>Origins</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Parenting</b>: Thyrsus,<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>:<br /> The legacy was founded in ancient Greece by cults dedicated to Dionysus and quickly spread throughout the western world. Although often derided, and sometimes even persecuted they have continued to thrive wherever people have gathered for hedonistic celebrations.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearances</b>:<br /> The fellowship vary wildly with the only real commonality being that they are almost always in the grip of mind altering drugs of some sort.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Doctrine</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Socialise 1, <br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b>:<br /> Initiation in the cult is pretty informal, mostly involving attending a celebratory revel to mark the occasion. The specifics vary depending on the makeup of the local cult, but &quot;hazing&quot; rituals reminiscent of college football initiations are not uncommon.<br /> <br /> <b>Organisation</b>:<br /> The fellowship are remarkably loose in organisation, with no form of hierarchy or strict rules amongst them. Nevertheless, where more than one gather for any length of time they tend to meet regularly for wild ecstatic rites. These are not generally closed affairs, and it is not uncommon for others to be invited along.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory</b>:<br /> Inheritors of the legacy of the Cults of Dionysus, these Ecstatics believe that a human must embrace their primal nature in order to find Ecstasy.<br /> They believe mankind is at its purest when in the grip of its unconsciousness, such as when drunk or making love or art, and tries to capture and harmonize with this unconscious beat.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Magic</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcana</b>: Fate<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras</b>:<br /> Having an alcoholic drink or taking a drug (+1)<br /> Being sufficiently inebriated to have the drugged condition (+2),<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations</b>:<br /> Engaging in revelry, partying, or celebrating with others. Engaging in purely hedonistic activities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>First attainment: Hedonistic Inspiration</b> <br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Fate 1, Initiation, socialise 1<br /> <i><b>Primary facto</b></i>r: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant<br /> <br /> By losing herself in hedonistic persuits and focusing on the ecstacy of bliss, a fellow of Pan may gain inspiration on the best course of action to take to accomplish a stated objective. On activation she receives a clear omen suggesting a course of action that will lead her closer to her goal. This seldom provides immediate success but can lead to an important breakthrough and is often found at the bottom of an empty glass.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Mind 1<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: discover aspiration and obsessions<br /> <br /> By spending a scene interactingwith their subject the fellow of Pan may come to understand them, discovering their virtue and vice as well and how many dots in mental and social attributes they have, as well as their aspirations and obsessions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Second attainment: Luck of the lost</b> <br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Fate 2, socialise 2<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: advanced duration, hour limit<br /> <br /> A fellow of Pan never lacks what they need for continued revelry and hedonism. By spending a scene engaged in hedonistic persuits, whatever they are looking for will cross their path within an hour.<br /> As long as whatever they are looking for could potentially appear I it will.<br /> The attainment can find someone with a specific trait, occupation, or context specific quality, but it always finds the closest or most available subject.<br /> Alternatively she temporarily gains access to a merit ( ally, contacts, resources, mentor, or retainer) with dots no greater than potency as she stumbles across dropped cash, unattended items, useful strangers etc.<br /> The merit may only be used a number of times equal to potency.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Mind 2<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: advanced duration<br /> <br /> By spending a scene becoming more immersed in the unconscious ecstacy that builds through the fellows activities she gains the ability to alter her basic mental flow, changing her subconscious thoughts and surface emanations to reflect any emotion she wishes. This sheild her from supernatural abilities that attempt to read her thoughts or Peirce her veil of lies and misdirections.<br /> Potency is added to relevant subterfuge rolls and supernatural powers that attempt to read her surface thoughts or emotions provoke a clash of wills.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Third attainment: Bumbling Competence</b> <br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Fate 3, socialise 3<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: change to potency, advanced duration, instant<br /> <br /> Fellows of Pan spend a lot of time either drunk or under the influence of drugs and despite the fact that they crash around with as little coordination or foresight as you would expect from someone who is out of their mind they retain a surprising degree of competence where it matters: stumbling out of the way of attacks, accidentally pressing the right buttons, hitting on just the right topic of conversation etc.<br /> This does not increase their competence above what it would normally be, but after an instant action to focus it does allow the attainments potency to cancel any penalties caused by the drugged condition on a number of actions equal to potency.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Mind 3<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant<br /> <br /> Inebriation and ecstacy break down barriers to language, just as surely as they break down barriers to action and by spending an instant action focusing a fellow can speak, read, and understand any language they can perceive.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fourth attainment: Go with the Flow</b><br /> <br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Fate 4, socialise 4<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant, advanced duration, add potency to mundane actions<br /> <br /> Fellows of Pan often act without planning or real preparation. So long as they have little detailed knowledge about a situation before they enter it they are able to act with perfect grace and timing, acting without conscious thoughts and allowing their actions to align perfectly with the flow of events. A turn or two studying the situation is fine, but detailed breifings or reconnaissance reduce the randomness that the attainment relies on. Luckily they rarely pay attention to such breifings anyway. They do not suffer untrained penalties for the duration of the attainment and may gain a bonus equal to potency on a number of rolls equal to potency.<br /> If the situation is a social one, their first impression also improves by 1.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Mind 4<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant, advanced scale, change to duration<br /> <i><b>Withstand</b></i>: Composure<br /> <br /> As they become one with the flow of events around them, ecstatic states of mind reached by Fellows of Pan become infectious allowing them to project emotional states at her subjects using the rules for advanced scale. She chooses to project a positive or negative emotion at the subject, opening or closing one door for the purposes of social manoeuvring. This does not have to benefit the fellow themselves, but can benefit anyone dealing with the subject during the duration of the spell. The fellow may also choose doors previously opened, making it harder for others to acheived their goals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fifth attainment: Dionysus Fulcrum</b><br /> <br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Fate 5, socialise 5<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: instant, affect spellcasting, advanced duration.<br /> <i><b>Withstand</b></i>: composure<br /> <br /> The fellow gains some control over the serendipitous events surrounding her, allowing her to bless our curse a subject with exceptional luck.<br /> This grants them either a boon or a hex which can affect spellcasting rolls.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Mind 5<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant, advanced duration<br /> <br /> The infectious nature of the fellows mental state expands allowing her to create false sensory input in her subject, tricking her senses and creating a hallucination that seems completely real to her subject. It affects sight, sound, taste, and smell but is unable to affect tactile senses.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-26T08:54:41-08:00","id":1503947,"title":"","content":"Completed the first draft of the Fellowship of Pan.<br /> <br /> I have noticed that I am terrible at naming attainments. I also struggle to find different oblations and yantra so there seems to be a lot of overlap between them. I am not sure if this is an issue.<br /> <br /> Prerequisites are another area I am unsure of. Are there guidelines about how demanding these should be?<br /> <br /> I ended up changing the ruling arcana from mind to fate as I was building it, because the fate attainments just feel more like the core practices of the cult. This leaves the optional Mind effects as an inferior arcanum for the Thyrsus path, but I guess they are just relatively rare in the cult.<br /> <br /> The second attainment pretty much just exists to counter the massive penalties from the drugged condition since it will be a common state for fellows of Pan, and they probably shouldn't be rendered completely ineffective by their core practices.<br /> <br /> It is based on Quantum flux which explicitly does not reduce penalties to spellcasting, but I felt that it was important that they should be effective casting magic under the influence as that is basically their whole purpose so I allowed it at the expense of limiting the attainments effects to purely that condition. I think that is a fair trade.<br /> As always I am grateful for any comments, advice, and critique.<br /> <br /> Next up are the kids of Astarte, but since they are another faction with very little given in the way of details I am tempted to skip them and return to them later. It depends on whether I can nail down a central theme for them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","user":"Tamuz","date":". 02-26-2023, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T02:40:05-08:00","id":1504191,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><u>Kiss of Astarte</u></b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Origins</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Parenting</b>: Thyrsus,<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>:<br /> They have been known by many names over the ages. Worshipped under the guise of many goddesses. Astarte, Ishtar, Innana, Aphrodite. Since the first civilisations there have been ecstatic cults revering a goddess of love and war (or more accurately, sex and violence). These cults saw the first sacred prostitutes drawing power from ritual sex, and the first preistesses empowered to wage war. Often challenging the grip of the underworld and death itself.<br /> Today they are most commonly named after Astarte, in whose name they fight and fuck in equal measure, rising high on a tide of ecstatic bliss.<br /> <br /> [Note that rather than the modern interpretation of Astarte as a feminist icon of female empowerment, I have gone with the more ancient (and probably less palatable) interpretations derived from Ishtar/Inanna. I also dropped the lesbian angle because I could find no historical sorry for it]<br /> <br /> <b>Appearances</b>:<br /> Most Astartites are female, although some of those are trans and there are a smattering of men most of whom are gay or bisexual. The cult is common amongst sex workers, and those who awaken reflect this. That said they are a widely varied group, with the only real commonality being that they are always seductive, and they are always dangerous.<br /> Doves are a common motif, sacred to many of the goddesses with whom they are associated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Doctrine</b></i><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: manipulation (seduction); brawl or weaponry<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Initiation into the cult invariably involves participation in ritual sex, and is rumoured to involve a martial test of some kind.<br /> <br /> <b>Organisation</b>:<br /> The legacy is organised thorough an ancient and hierarchical cult.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory</b>:<br /> The astartites prefer to approach ecstacy through the intimacy of shared communion. They build their partners to an extasy of shared sexual climax, using them as tools through which they can see past the lie and reach for the supernal. A similar moment of ecstatic truth can be found at the moment of death, and while it loses the power and immediacy of intimate communion, war can replicate this symbolically on a huge scale.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Magic</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcana</b>: Life<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras</b>:<br /> Intimate contact (+1)<br /> Sex (+2) can only be used for ritual casting<br /> Sacrificing a dove (+1)<br /> Killing an enemy (+2)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Oblations</b>:<br /> Having sex, preparing a war or violent confrontation, entering and returning from the underworld<br /> <b>First attainment</b>: <b>Sensual awareness</b><br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Life 1, Initiation,<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: advanced duration<br /> By spending a scene (probably off stage) engaging in intimate activities that center her awareness on her senses, the astartite can heighten her senses becoming intimately aware of the world around her<br /> and gaining a bonus to perception equal to potency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Death 1 - spiritual awareness<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: instant<br /> <br /> Astartites are able to see and speak with ghosts, enabling them to interrogate the fallen, and even enlist their side at times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Second attainment: Embodiment of Astarte</b><br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Life 2,<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: advanced duration<br /> <br /> By spending a scene enacting erotic rituals, the astartite embodies the supernal truth of the warrior goddess, gaining complete control of her bodily functions. Each level of potency gives a rank in the breathing, metabolism, reflexes, and scent, and healing aspects as per the spell &quot;body control&quot;.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Death 2 - Astartes Sheild<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: duration<br /> <b><i>Reach</i></b>: instant<br /> <br /> Astarte and her predecessors are rumoured to have journeyed into the underworld itself, proving that death had no hooks over then t. Astrtites are well prepared for similar journeys, gaining protection from ghostly numina, influence, manifestations, death spells, and death related powers of other supernatural creatures. Powers attempting to Peirce the sheild provoke a clash of wills.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Third attainment: Form of Astarte</b><br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Life 3,<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant<br /> <br /> In both love and war, appearances can be paramount. The Astartite learns to mold her form to whatever is needed, becoming more beautiful or more terrifying in an instant.<br /> Within the confines of species and age, she may transform however she wishes altering any physical aspects of her body.<br /> She may also redistribute her physical or social dots as she sees fit so long as none go below 0 or above her maximum.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Death 3 - Shadow Armoury<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: instant<br /> <br /> An astartite is never entirely unarmed. She can mold and shape Shadows into physical items with a durability of 2. Weapons have and armour have a rating of 2, otherwise equipment gains a rating of 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fourth attainment: Curse of Astarte</b><br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Life 4<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: advanced duration, instant<br /> <br /> The Astartite may withdraw the goddess favour from her target, reducing their abilities to wage war and make love.<br /> One of the targets physical or social attributes is reduced by one dot for each level of potency.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Death 4 - Sexual Vampire<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: instant, may affect healthy individuals<br /> <i><b>Withstand</b></i>: resolve<br /> <br /> The Astartite may pull energy from the subjects ecstatic experiences into herself. If a subject is experiencing excruciating pain, death throes, or orgasmic pleasure, the mage may harvest willpower or scourge the subjects pattern for mana.<br /> For each level of potency the mage may take 1 point of willpower or scour the subjects pattern for 1 point of mana, causing a lethal wound in the process.<br /> This counts towards the number of times per day the mage can gain mana through scouring.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth attainment: Goddess of War</b><br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Life 5<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: instant, sensory range, advanced duration, affect supernatural creatures.<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>composure<br /> <br /> The seductive influence of the Astartite overrides even the strongest wills and with a simple gesture she can render opponents slaves to their impulses.<br /> <br /> This operates as the spell &quot;control instincts&quot; <br /> <br /> <i><b>Optional</b></i>: Death 5 - Open the gates<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: instant<br /> <br /> Just as the goddess returned from the underworld, so too can the Astartite fling open the gates of death, creating an iris between the material world and the upper layer of the underworld within the area of effect. Opening the gate causes the area to gain a death resonance and the gateway condition for the duration of the effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","user":"Tamuz","date":". 03-07-2023, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T02:56:58-08:00","id":1504194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1504191#post1504191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><u>Kiss of Astarte</u></b></span></div><u><b>Origins</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Parenting</b>: Thyrsus,<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>:<br /> They have been known by many names over the ages. Worshipped under the guise of many goddesses. Astarte, Ishtar, Innana, Aphrodite. Since the first civilisations there have been ecstatic cults revering a goddess of love and war (or more accurately, sex and violence). These cults saw the first sacred prostitutes drawing power from ritual sex, and the first preistesses empowered to wage war. Often challenging the grip of the underworld and death itself.<br /> Today they are most commonly named after Astarte, in whose name they fight and fuck in equal measure, rising high on a tide of ecstatic bliss.<br /> <br /> [Note that rather than the modern interpretation of Astarte as a feminist icon of female empowerment, I have gone with the more ancient (and probably less palatable) interpretations derived from Ishtar/Inanna. I also dropped the lesbian angle because I could find no historical sorry for it]<br /> <br /> <b>Appearances</b>:<br /> Most Astartites are female, although some of those are trans and there are a smattering of men most of whom are gay or bisexual. The cult is common amongst sex workers, and those who awaken reflect this. That said they are a widely varied group, with the only real commonality being that they are always seductive, and they are always dangerous.<br /> Doves are a common motif, sacred to many of the goddesses with whom they are associated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><b>Doctrine</b></i><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: manipulation (seduction); brawl or weaponry<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Initiation into the cult invariably involves participation in ritual sex, and is rumoured to involve a martial test of some kind.<br /> <br /> <b>Organisation</b>:<br /> The legacy is organised thorough an ancient and hierarchical cult.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory</b>:<br /> The astartites prefer to approach ecstacy through the intimacy of shared communion. They build their partners to an extasy of shared sexual climax, using them as tools through which they can see past the lie and reach for the supernal. A similar moment of ecstatic truth can be found at the moment of death, and while it loses the power and immediacy of intimate communion, war can replicate this symbolically on a huge scale.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Magic</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcana</b>: Life<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras</b>:<br /> Intimate contact (+1)<br /> Sex (+2) can only be used for ritual casting<br /> Sacrificing a dove (+1)<br /> Killing an enemy (+2)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Oblations</b>:<br /> Having sex, preparing a war or violent confrontation, entering and returning from the underworld</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Yantras, can the sex be with their enemy who is also killed during the ritual to use two (+2) yantras?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-02T12:50:30-08:00","id":1504221,"title":"","content":"Yes. Although it would be more than a little bit rapey. One thing that you have to remember with Ecstatics is that a big part of what they do is deliberately push beyond social boundaries.<br /> <br /> Hell, given the cults association with the underworld and the lands of the dead the sex party might not even come before the killing part.<br /> <br /> Historical factions pushed past social boundaries that would already have seemed extreme to modern sensibilities. The cults of Inanna/Ishtar and Astarte live in a world where lives were brutally short and might made right.<br /> <br /> The practices of historical ecstatic factions in particular (and ecstatic factions in general) probably shouldn't be comfortable or even palatable.<br /> <br /> The only thing keeping the kiss of Astarte from being considered left handed is probably the fact that they fight on behalf of local consilium.<br /> <br /> The next group are probably just as uncomfortable in many ways - Maenads are a bit like a (mostly female, again - I'm starting to see a trend here) sociopathically murderous version of the fellowship of Pan. Good times.<br /> <br /> I doubt modern legacy holders from these historical factions would be especially common or widespread in the modern world - more like little pockets of cultural preservation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T10:39:12-08:00","id":1504274,"title":"","content":"A quick bit of feedback on the formatting, including the name of the spell that the Attainment replicates makes it much easier to read. In the second optional Attainment, for example, you could have dedicated the first paragraph explain the flavor and how to activate it, the on the next one write something along the lines of &quot;This replicates <i>Ghost Shield</i>, with Reach assigned to instant use&quot;, which makes it both concise and easier for players to reference during sessions. In case of custom spells, I recommend the format &quot;This is a [Practice] of [Arcana] utilizing the purview of [chosen Arcana's purview] to [explanation on how its possible], with Reach assigned to [chosen factors]&quot;.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Attainments themselves, the beauty and seduction angle do not seem to flow in a way that would be practical in and out of the battlefield. An example would be the last Life Attainment, utilizing <i>Control Instincts</i> with Reach to instant use, sensory range, advanced duration and affecting supernatural beings would make it have a powerful effect both in conversation and battle. <i>Honing The Form, </i>in contrast, could be cast as a ritual as the 4th Attainment, utilizing the Reach for advanced duration and going beyond trait limits.<br /> <br /> While <i>Ghost Gate</i> is useful for a quick getaway, but it doesn't have the same offensive power as for example, a spell that makes emits ectoplasm that is then transformed into a Safe Place. This would use a Patterning of Life and Death to replicate <i>Spirit Manse</i>, allowing it to take the form of an idyllic natural home (aspect of seduction) or a dense jungle that aids them in their hunt (aspect of war).<br /> <br /> Your explanation invokes a sense of utilitarian, primal beauty. But how they view combat is not very clear when looking at the Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-03-2023, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-03T21:36:52-08:00","id":1504332,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the feedback.<br /> <br /> I was wondering about how to format the attainments. I will format them as you suggest from now on, and as and when I find time I will go back and reformat the ones I have done.<br /> <br /> I will have a think about your suggestions on the attainments. To be honest I was struggling with them. Control instincts is certainly tempting as it was something that leapt out at me from the start as something that is thematic. I think joining the form could probably be dropped as I'm not sure it adds much over the ability to swap dots around from many faces. <br /> <br /> Ghost Gate was mainly thematic, drawing from the stories of the goddess traveling into the underworld, but I can see the utility of creating a manse instead, so will certainly consider it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T02:03:57-08:00","id":1504824,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><u><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Maenads</span></u></b></div> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Origins</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Parenting</b>: Thyrsus,<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>:<br /> The Maenads have long been associated with violence, ferocity, and Madness. They worship Dionysus through bloody rites in which women gather under the full moon to take drugs and engage in wild dancing that becomes more frenzied and out of control as the night goes on, inevitably culminating in bloody death as their prey is torn apart and offered as sacrifice.<br /> Even more concerning is that this madness is not contained within the legacy itself, often spreading to others nearby and on occasion tainting whole communities.<br /> Modern maenads operate with more subtlety than their ancestral sisters, often finding much common ground with their fellow worshipers of Dionysus in the fellowship of Pan. Their savagery remains however and the only thing stopping the entire legacy from being declared left handed is that where possible they direct their murderous passions towards enemies of the local consilium, and where not they hunt animals or spirits. Nevertheless, their practices take an inevitable toll on their wisdom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Appearances</b>:<br /> Maenads are violent, wild, and unpredictable. Sometimes they manage to maintain a facade of normalcy, but more often they find themselves drifting to the fringes of society - especially those fringes where violence is considered acceptable.<br /> <br /> <b>Doctrine</b><br /> Despite their (deserved) reputation for violence, the Maenads focus is on finding ecstacy through wild uninhibited abandon. Their rites involve as much drinking, drug taking, and sex as they do violence - violence is just such a depressingly inevitable end point that it quickly became so synonymous with the cult that it shaped their own identity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>:<br /> Brawl, athletics, (feels like there should be a merit representing status in a spirit court) spirit allies would not go amiss, secret society status<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation</b>:<br /> A prospective Maenad is invited to participate in a full moon party where she experiences possession by a spirit and learns to completely let go of her inhibitions and sense of self.<br /> <br /> <b>Organisation</b>:<br /> The Maenads meet every full moon to enact their rites although these are not always the violent spectacle their reputation paints in people's minds and sometimes they are little more than wild parties.<br /> Sleeper cults are surprisingly common amongst the legacy, with sleeper worshippers often becoming possessed by the spirits that flock to surround the cults activities.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory</b>:<br /> Inhibitions, expectations, and restraint are products of the lie. By deliberately letting go of those restrictions and acting out their wildest impulses they free themselves from the hold of the fallen world and embody the higher symbolism of the primal wilds.<br /> Over time the legacy have gained allies among spirits of ecstacy, inhibition, and savagery who they work alongside to shatter the false restraints of the fallen world.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Magic</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcana</b>: Spirit<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras</b>:<br /> Wild dancing (+2 but only used in rituals)<br /> Full moon (+1)<br /> Breaking social taboos (+1)<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations</b>:<br /> Acting without inhibition in a dangerous or antisocial fashion, encouraging wild behaviour in others,<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>First attainment</b>: <b>Sight of the Wild</b><br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Spirit 1, initiation<br /> <i><b>Primary factor:</b></i> Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant<br /> <br /> By releasing her inhibitions and opening herself to the instincts of the primal wild, a Maenad is able to open her senses to the spiritual realities of the world around her.<br /> This functions identically to Exorcists eye.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 1<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: instant<br /> <br /> The primal wild resonates with life within the fallen world and by watching it's pulse as the lie falls away the Maenad can sense living beings nearby.<br /> This functions identically to Web of Life<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Second attainment: Primitive Liberation</b><br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Spirit 2<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: instant<br /> <br /> Spirits flock to the resonance generated by Maenad rites and Maenads quickly learn how to open the way for them to manifest or hold them from the material world. Generally this is used to make manifestation easier, allowing the spirits a foothold in the material world, thereby spreading the madness of their rites and damaging the lie.<br /> This functions identically to opener of the way.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 2<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: instant<br /> Maenads use drink, drugs, and other intoxicants to help lower inhibitions and ease themselves into States of ecstatic savagery. When needed however they quickly sharpen up, denying intoxicants a good of them just as easily as they can deny spirits. Dangerously wild but without a hint of the intoxication that brought them to this point.<br /> This functions identically to cleanse the body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Third attainment</b>: <b>Abandonment of Fetters</b><br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Spirit 3<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Duration<br /> <br /> By spending a scene leading wild ecstatic rites the Maenad can erode the lies and inhibitions that separate the fallen world from the shadow, and by doing so bring the world closer to the primal wild itself.<br /> This functions identically to place of power<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 3<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Potency<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant<br /> Maenads not only erode the lies that separate the shadow, but also those that restrict her with minor injuries, leaving her wound behind along with her inhibitions.<br /> This functions identically to Knit<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fourth attainment</b>: <b>Inhibitions Unbound </b><br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Spirit 4<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: instant , advanced duration, sensory casting<br /> <i><b>Withstand</b></i>: Rank<br /> Through surrendering to the savagery of her primal instincts a Maenad eventually gains some measure of control over the wild rites she oversees. In doing so she also gains a measure of control over the spirits drawn to those rites.<br /> This functions identically to command spirit<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 4<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant, advanced duration, sensory casting.<br /> <i><b>Withstand</b></i>: Composure<br /> Maenads gain control not only over spirits, but also the instinctual acts of those caught up in her rites.<br /> This functions identically to control instincts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fifth attainment: Queen of Shadows</b><br /> <i><b>Prerequisites</b></i>: Spirit 5<br /> <i><b>Primary factor</b></i>: duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: advanced duration<br /> <i><b>Practice</b></i>: Making<br /> <br /> At the pinnacle of her art the Maenad takes a position of rulership amongst the spirits flocking to her rites,<br /> giving her a rank amongst spirits no higher than her spirit arcana.<br /> Spirits of lesser rank may seek (or be persuaded) to attach themselves to the Maenads court and she is treated with the honour and dignity due to get station (and expected to uphold the etiquette of the courts).<br /> When calling, controlling, binding, or otherwise using sympathetic magic on members of her court the mage may cast spells as if the spirits were in intimate sympathetic contact with her without need of the side Arcanum.<br /> Any spiritual alliances the Maenad makes are rendered null and void when the spell expires (but she will be expected to uphold her obligations). It is common for Maenads to enact the rites to renew their court regularly.<br /> (This functions in the same manner as the 1ed spell spirit court).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 5<br /> <i><b>Primary</b></i>: Duration<br /> <i><b>Reach</b></i>: Instant, advanced duration, raise attribute above max<br /> <br /> Drawing on the power of her court, the Maenad becomes faster, stronger, and tougher.<br /> <br /> This functions identically to honing the form","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","user":"Tamuz","date":". 03-08-2023, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-08T02:10:42-08:00","id":1504825,"title":"","content":"Completed the first draft of the Maenads. I have not named the attainments yet but overall I am happier with this one than I was with the kiss of Astarte even if it ended up going in a slightly different direction than I originally envisioned.<br /> <br /> I Considered mind for the madness and spreading madness angle but looking through things spirit just seemed to fit better.<br /> <br /> I am still considering changes to the Astarte attainments and will revisit them as I get my head around things. I don't think they seem as thematically streamlined as the two Dionysus cults, which I think is causing problems.<br /> <br /> As always, comments, criticisms, suggestions, and alternative takes are welcome.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I have added some names for the attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":14453,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","user":"Tamuz","date":". 03-08-2023, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T04:28:21-07:00","id":1505481,"title":"","content":"A <b>Legacie on the fires of passion?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27472-phoenix853457","name":"Phoenix853457","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27472_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-16T16:53:32-07:00","id":1505515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tamuz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503450-awakening-the-traditions-sahajiya?p=1504221#post1504221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that you have to remember with Ecstatics is that a big part of what they do is deliberately push beyond social boundaries.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the by, that aspect is a perfect fit for the Mastigos as a parent path. They focus on deliberate violations of taboos and such as part of their path.<br /> <br /> The experiential aspect is very Thyrsus, so I'm not saying these don't fit, but you can actually mix and match with any of the paths:<br /> <br /> Transcending crude mortal matter and shackles to the physical is a Moros focus.<br /> <br /> Acanthus study fate and intuition. They are associated with faeries. Ecstasy fits their path to the Mysteries.<br /> <br /> The Obrimos include ascetics who strive to bring their fleshly desires into the divine will through ecstatic practice.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not knocking what you're up to, but you might find that some of the other paths actually fit better and that's perfectly fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T11:51:37-07:00","id":1506331,"title":"","content":"Interesting. If you think any of the specific legacies I have done for another path better then let me know and I will take a look.<br /> <br /> Coming up down the line are the Hagalaz (actually 3 legacies based on norse mythology) whom I was already considering other paths might be a better fit. Mostly Acanthus.<br /> <br /> I have stalled on the Kan Lu and the Vajrapani as I have absolutely no idea what to do with them (or no way to choose between competing ideas) so they have been put on a back burner.<br /> <br /> Next up will be the Aghori - based on the Indian cults worshipping Shakti and Khali. I was considering that mastigos or moros might be a good fit for them so will give it some thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}